        "root_concepts": "[untranslatability]",
        "section": "translation",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Untranslatability and the Limits of Language",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "**The project**: A dictionary of philosophical terms that resist translation — not because they are obscure, but because they do conceptual work in their original language that no single word in another language replicates."
    },
    {
      "id": "06-UNTRANSLATABILITY.md#008",
      "path": [
        "06-UNTRANSLATABILITY.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[proof-backfill:translation:06-untranslatability, git-history:translation:06-untranslatability]",
        "canonical_path": "translation/06-UNTRANSLATABILITY.md",
