        "current_path": "translation/06-UNTRANSLATABILITY.md",
        "id": "maxim:translation:untranslatability",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "translation",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[untranslatability]",
        "section": "translation",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Untranslatability and the Limits of Language",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "**Key concept**: The untranslatable is not something that *cannot* be translated (everything can be explained in any language); it is something that *one keeps on translating* — a symptom of the untranslatable is that it requires re-translation, because no single rendering is adequate."
    },
