        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Untranslatability and the Limits of Language",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "GERMAN: Stimmung\n  Standard English rendering: \"mood,\" \"atmosphere,\" \"attunement\"\n  What it means: The tonal quality of a space or experience;\n  Heidegger's use: our primordial openness to Being; the way\n  we are always \"attuned\" to the world before deliberate thought.\n  Why \"mood\" fails: Stimmung in German derives from Stimme (voice)\n  and Stimmen (to tune an instrument). The harmony/tuning\n  metaphor is present and meaningful. \"Mood\" is purely\n  psychological; Stimmung is ontological."
    },
    {
      "id": "06-UNTRANSLATABILITY.md#011",
      "path": [
        "06-UNTRANSLATABILITY.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[proof-backfill:translation:06-untranslatability, git-history:translation:06-untranslatability]",
        "canonical_path": "translation/06-UNTRANSLATABILITY.md",
        "concepts": "[untranslatability]",
        "current_path": "translation/06-UNTRANSLATABILITY.md",
        "id": "maxim:translation:untranslatability",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "translation",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[untranslatability]",
        "section": "translation",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Untranslatability and the Limits of Language",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "GERMAN: Dasein\n  Standard rendering: \"Being-there,\" \"existence,\" \"human reality\"\n  (Sartre used the French: \"réalité humaine\" — Heidegger objected)\n  What it means: For Heidegger: the kind of being that humans are —\n  characterized by thrown, temporal, relational existence.\n  Not \"a subject\" or \"a consciousness\"; the very mode of existing.\n  Why untranslatable: Anglophone philosophy has adopted \"Dasein\"\n  as a loan word — the most common resolution."
    },
    {
      "id": "06-UNTRANSLATABILITY.md#012",
      "path": [
        "06-UNTRANSLATABILITY.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[proof-backfill:translation:06-untranslatability, git-history:translation:06-untranslatability]",
