        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Untranslatability and the Limits of Language",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "FRENCH: Esprit\n  Renderings: \"spirit,\" \"mind,\" \"wit,\" \"intelligence\"\n  What it means: Covers what English distributes between \"spirit\"\n  (spiritual/religious), \"mind\" (cognitive), and \"wit\" (clever).\n  Esprit de corps: rendered \"esprit de corps\" in English —\n  English borrowed the whole phrase."
    },
