        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Untranslatability and the Limits of Language",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "STRONG VERSION (Linguistic Determinism):\n  You cannot think thoughts that your language cannot\n  express. People who speak languages without tense\n  cannot conceptualize time.\n  Status: REJECTED by modern linguistics and psychology.\n  Evidence against: Bilingual speakers can think in\n  both frameworks; language acquisition shows children\n  have prelinguistic concepts."
    },
    {
      "id": "06-UNTRANSLATABILITY.md#020",
      "path": [
        "06-UNTRANSLATABILITY.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[proof-backfill:translation:06-untranslatability, git-history:translation:06-untranslatability]",
        "canonical_path": "translation/06-UNTRANSLATABILITY.md",
